# libssl3 -- CVE-2026-84782
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full, stats-cluster
# DTLS retransmission logic flaw in OpenSSL. DTLS is TLS over UDP (WebRTC, CoAP,
# some VPNs); datawatch's containers serve and call only regular TCP-based
# TLS/HTTPS, never originating or accepting a DTLS connection -- the flawed code
# path is never reached. Phase 1's live rescan found this spans all 5 images,
# not only stats-cluster as originally scoped when it blocked v8.35.0's release
# CI.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
CVE-2026-84782

# python3.11, libpython3.11-* -- CVE-2026-19553
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-gemini
# Certificate verification bypass via missing server_hostname validation in
# ssl.SSLContext.wrap_bio(). Whether agent-gemini's Python runtime actually
# calls wrap_bio() (vs. the higher-level wrap_socket()/create_default_context()
# paths most HTTP clients use, which are unaffected) was not independently
# traced before suppressing -- only that no Debian fix exists.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm. NOT independently traced (self-admitted
# caveat) -- re-review should actually trace which TLS call path agent-gemini's
# code uses, the way CVE-2026-19445 was traced this session.
CVE-2026-19553

# libpython3.11-minimal -- CVE-2026-19445
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-gemini
# Use-after-free of a server-side SSLContext when sni_callback switches contexts
# mid-handshake (3.11.2-6+deb12u9). Grepped every installed Python package
# (stdlib + both images' full site-packages, including agent-aider's pipx venv)
# for sni_callback: zero hits anywhere except the stdlib's own ssl.py attribute
# definition. aiohttp.worker does build a server-side SSLContext, but the only
# aiohttp importers found in agent-aider are Google auth's async client
# transport wrappers, not a server. The vulnerable code path is confirmed
# unreachable.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm. Independently traced and confirmed
# unreachable this session -- re-check for a fix each cycle; re-trace only if
# either tool's dependency tree changes meaningfully.
# TRACED: grep of installed site-packages in networkless container (docker run
# --entrypoint /bin/sh --network none)
CVE-2026-19445

# openjdk-17-jre-headless -- CVE-2026-114820
# severity: high; images: parent-full
# The JRE is installed in parent-full only to run signal-cli
# (Dockerfile.parent-full). A source trace shows java is started only by
# internal/signal (signalcli.go, javafix.go). CVE-2026-114820 is an Oracle Java
# SE advisory (2026-10-24) in the JSSE component, CVSS 3.1 9.1, exploitable over
# the network through APIs that process TLS data. signal-cli uses JSSE as a TLS
# client to the Signal service; datawatch starts it with a local config
# directory and does not expose a TLS listener from the JVM, and the container
# publishes no JVM port. An attacker would therefore have to be a hostile TLS
# peer of signal-cli (the Signal service endpoints or a man in the middle of
# that connection), which signal-cli's pinned trust store makes difficult, but
# the client-side code path is real and the vulnerable APIs were not traced
# further, so reachability is recorded as unknown rather than no. Messaging over
# Signal is an optional feature; the image is not used without it.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm:
# security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-114820 (checked 2026-10-30) lists
# bookworm security 17.0.21+9-1~deb12u1 as vulnerable; fixed only in sid
# (17.0.21.0.3+1-1). Found live by the v9.39.0 Release workflow blocking
# parent-full scan. Short expiry: re-check every few days and consume the Debian
# update as soon as it ships (security patches are consumed when available).
# TRACED: source grep of every java invocation in the repository (source trace;
# not a container linker scan); CVE description read on NVD and the Debian
# security tracker, 2026-10-30
CVE-2026-114820

# libsqlite3-0 -- CVE-2026-119373
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# The finding is a denial of service through a heap based buffer problem in
# SQLite, which needs attacker supplied SQL text or a crafted database file
# handed to the library. The recorded trace of this library shows that in
# agent-base the only binary linking libsqlite3-0 is gpg (its trust database),
# nothing in datawatch invokes gpg at runtime, git, apt, curl, tmux and openssh
# do not link it, datawatch itself uses the pure Go modernc.org/sqlite driver
# built without cgo so it never loads the system library, agent-aider adds
# python3 whose sqlite3 module runs fixed SQL only, and agent-gemini and
# parent-full add no other consumer. No path gives an attacker control of SQL
# text or a database file for the system library. This is reasoning from the
# earlier trace, not a new trace, so it expires in 30 days.
# The Trivy scan of agent-base in the 9.58.0 Release run lists CVE-2026-119373
# (HIGH) on libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 as affected with no fixed version;
# re-check security-tracker.debian.org for a bookworm fix each release and
# re-trace if gpg or python start handling untrusted databases.
CVE-2026-119373

# libexpat1 -- CVE-2026-117610
# severity: high; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# A NULL pointer dereference in libexpat (through 2.9.0), a crash of the process
# that parses a crafted XML document. It needs attacker supplied XML handed to
# the parser. In agent-base the only package that depends on libexpat1 is git,
# and the only git program that links it is git-http-push, the WebDAV push
# helper. datawatch clones and pushes over ssh and over smart HTTPS to
# configured remotes and never runs git-http-push, so no XML from a remote
# reaches the parser. The Python XML parser in the aider image is a separate
# finding (CVE-2026-7210) accepted on its own entry.
# The Trivy scan of agent-base in the 9.64.1 Release run lists CVE-2026-117610
# (HIGH) on libexpat1 2.5.0-1+deb12u5 as affected with no fixed version;
# re-check security-tracker.debian.org for a bookworm fix each release and
# remove this entry when one ships.
# TRACED: docker run --network none on a built agent-base image: apt-cache
# rdepends --installed libexpat1 lists only git; ldd of /usr/bin/git,
# /usr/lib/git-core/git-remote-http and /usr/lib/git-core/git-http-push shows
# that only git-http-push links libexpat. The installed expat in that image was
# 2.5.0-1+deb12u4, the same package family as the scanned 2.5.0-1+deb12u5.
CVE-2026-117610

