# git -- CVE-2026-105437
# severity: high; images: agent-base
# CVE-2026-105437 is a heap buffer overflow in git's three-way merge code
# (xdiff): an oversized conflict-marker-size value from a repository's
# attributes makes a 32-bit size total wrap, so a merge that hits a conflict can
# write past a too-small buffer. It needs git to run a merge on a repository the
# attacker controls. NOT traced inside a built image (no docker run was done).
# From reading the source: the agent-base Dockerfile installs git (plus git-lfs)
# from apt as a dependency of the agent tooling, and also uses git only at build
# time to clone the pinned cli/cli tag in the ghbuilder stage. Code in
# internal/agents/worker_clone.go, which runs in the worker, only clones, runs
# rev-parse and pushes; none of those run xdiff merges. The only git merge calls
# found in the repo (internal/autonomous/task_merge.go) are made by the
# datawatch daemon on the operator's own task worktree branches, not by a
# process inside agent-base. Not ruled out: an agent running inside the
# container (an LLM coding session) could run git merge, pull or rebase in the
# checked-out project repository, whose content the operator chose to clone;
# that is why reachable is unknown rather than no.
# The Trivy scan of agent-base in the Release workflow lists CVE-2026-105437
# (HIGH) on git 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3 as affected with no fixed version; the Debian
# security tracker (read 2026-11-13) lists bookworm (deb12u3 and
# bookworm-security deb12u2), trixie and sid as vulnerable with no fixed version
# (sid source is unfixed); untraced so the 30-day cap applies; re-check
# security-tracker.debian.org each release and remove this entry when a fix
# ships.
CVE-2026-105437

# git, git-man -- CVE-2026-111760
# severity: high; images: agent-base
# CVE-2026-111760 is an integer truncation in git's index path handling: a very
# long path validates as one name and is written as a shorter one, so an
# attacker-controlled repository can replace a submodule's .git file with a
# symlink to a directory holding malicious config or hooks, and git then runs
# attacker code during a RECURSIVE clone. NOT traced inside a built image (no
# docker run was done); the analysis is from reading the Debian tracker,
# upstream advisories and the source. The datawatch worker bootstrap in
# internal/agents/worker_clone.go runs a plain non-recursive git clone (no
# --recurse-submodules, no submodule update) of the operator-configured project
# URL, plus checkout, rev-parse, pull --ff-only, remote set-url and push.
# Nothing in docker, internal, cmd, scripts or .github runs git fast-import or
# fast-export. The build-time clone of the pinned gh tag happens only in the
# ghbuilder stage, not in the runtime image. Residual risk that is NOT ruled
# out: an agent session (an LLM coding session) running inside agent-base can
# run any git command, including a recursive clone of an untrusted third-party
# repository, or git submodule update --init --recursive, on such a repository.
# The image has no baked gitconfig and none is claimed as a mitigation. Both
# CVEs share Debian bug 1153670; upstream fixed them in git 2.56.1 and the
# 2.55.1, 2.54.1, 2.53.1, 2.52.1, 2.51.3 and 2.50.2 backports, which Debian has
# not packaged yet.
# The Release scan of agent-base 9.171.1 lists CVE-2026-111760 (HIGH) on git and
# git-man 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3 as affected with no fixed version; the Debian
# security tracker (read 2026-11-13) lists bookworm, bookworm-security, trixie,
# forky and sid as vulnerable with no fix; untraced so the 30-day cap applies;
# the image's apt-get upgrade picks up a Debian fix when it ships, so remove
# this entry then; near expiry, renew or build git from source in a pinned
# stage.
CVE-2026-111760

# git, git-man -- CVE-2026-114466
# severity: high; images: agent-base
# CVE-2026-114466 is in git fast-import and fast-export: the
# rewrite-submodules-from/to features (arbitrary file read) and
# export-pack-edges (file create or append) are not blocked for an untrusted
# stream, so it matters only when git processes an untrusted fast-import stream.
# NOT traced inside a built image (no docker run was done); the analysis is from
# reading the Debian tracker, upstream advisories and the source. The datawatch
# worker bootstrap in internal/agents/worker_clone.go runs a plain non-recursive
# git clone (no --recurse-submodules, no submodule update) of the
# operator-configured project URL, plus checkout, rev-parse, pull --ff-only,
# remote set-url and push. Nothing in docker, internal, cmd, scripts or .github
# runs git fast-import or fast-export. The build-time clone of the pinned gh tag
# happens only in the ghbuilder stage, not in the runtime image. Residual risk
# that is NOT ruled out: an agent session (an LLM coding session) running inside
# agent-base can run any git command, including a recursive clone of an
# untrusted third-party repository, or feed an untrusted stream to git
# fast-import. The image has no baked gitconfig and none is claimed as a
# mitigation. Both CVEs share Debian bug 1153670; upstream fixed them in git
# 2.56.1 and the 2.55.1, 2.54.1, 2.53.1, 2.52.1, 2.51.3 and 2.50.2 backports,
# which Debian has not packaged yet.
# The Release scan of agent-base 9.171.1 lists CVE-2026-114466 (HIGH) on git and
# git-man 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3 as affected with no fixed version; the Debian
# security tracker (read 2026-11-13) lists bookworm, bookworm-security, trixie,
# forky and sid as vulnerable with no fix; untraced so the 30-day cap applies;
# the image's apt-get upgrade picks up a Debian fix when it ships, so remove
# this entry then; near expiry, renew or build git from source in a pinned
# stage.
CVE-2026-114466

# soupsieve -- CVE-2026-126190
# severity: high; images: agent-aider
# CVE-2026-126190 is a polynomial-time denial of service (ReDoS) in Soup Sieve's
# CSS selector handling, so it is only triggered when an attacker controls the
# selector string passed to soupsieve (through bs4's select or select_one).
# Aider uses beautifulsoup4 only to scrape pages it fetches itself and its own
# code contains no select, select_one or soupsieve call, so no selector string,
# attacker-controlled or not, reaches soupsieve from aider. Page content cannot
# supply a selector. Not patched because the fixed soupsieve (4.0.0) requires
# Python >=3.11.5, as does every release from 3.0.2 on, and the image runs
# Debian 12's Python 3.11.2, so pip refuses it. Forcing it with
# --ignore-requires-python is not done because upstream yanked 3.0 and 3.0.1 for
# breakage on older Pythons. Cleared by moving the aider venv to Python >=3.11.5
# (follow-up filed separately), after which soupsieve can be upgraded and this
# entry removed.
# The Release scan of agent-aider lists CVE-2026-126190 (HIGH) on soupsieve
# 2.10, fixed in 4.0.0, which needs Python >=3.11.5 while the image has 3.11.2;
# accepted for 30 days; remove when the aider venv moves to Python >=3.11.5 and
# soupsieve is upgraded.
# TRACED: docker run --network none --entrypoint sh on the local
# dw-verify-agent-aider:test image (Python 3.11.2, aider-chat 0.86.0,
# beautifulsoup4 4.13.4, soupsieve 2.10; the same pins as
# docker/dockerfiles/Dockerfile.agent-aider, but this local image was not built
# from main today): grep of the aider package in the aider-chat venv
# site-packages for .select(, select_one, soupsieve and .css. finds no call; the
# only users of soupsieve in the venv outside its own package are bs4 itself
# (bs4/css.py, element.py, builder/_lxml.py) and bs4's tests.
CVE-2026-126190

# soupsieve -- CVE-2026-126191
# severity: high; images: agent-aider
# CVE-2026-126191 is an exponential-time denial of service (ReDoS) in Soup
# Sieve's selector compilation, so it is only triggered when an attacker
# controls the selector string passed to soupsieve (through bs4's select or
# select_one). The earlier trace for CVE-2026-126190 found no select, select_one
# or soupsieve call in aider; that finding is reused here and was not re-traced,
# so this entry is untraced and the 30-day cap applies. Not patched because the
# fixed soupsieve (3.0.2) requires Python >=3.11.5, as does every release from
# 3.0.2 on, and the image runs Debian 12's Python 3.11.2, so pip refuses it.
# Cleared by moving the aider venv to Python >=3.11.5 (Automaton 66dd0001),
# after which soupsieve can be upgraded and this entry removed.
# The Release scan of agent-aider lists CVE-2026-126191 (HIGH, exponential ReDoS
# in selector compilation) on soupsieve 2.10, fixed in 3.0.2, which needs Python
# >=3.11.5 while the image has 3.11.2; accepted for 30 days, untraced (impact
# reused from CVE-2026-126190); remove when the aider venv moves to Python
# >=3.11.5 (Automaton 66dd0001) and soupsieve is upgraded.
CVE-2026-126191
